# What each of Urdu's own characters arrives as: the code point a caller
# writes, and the byte its alphabet knows that character by. The bytes were
# free in the alphabet Italian brought; tools/module/alphabet.py show urpk
# says what each one is now.
#
# One byte per sound rather than per letter. Urdu writes one sound several
# ways -- s three, z four -- and there were fifty bytes free, which is not a
# letter each. Letters that sound the same share a byte, which costs the
# engine being able to tell them apart when spelling a word out and costs
# nothing when saying one.
#
# The letters and their sounds are from references/g2ps/Urdu, which is MIT.
# Where Urdu makes a distinction this chassis has not got -- the retroflexes,
# the aspirates, /h/, /x/, /q/ -- the letter has a byte of its own so a rule
# can see it later, and the nearest sound Italian has until then.

0621 1d   # ain and hamza, both silent here
0622 0b   # alef and alef madda
0627 0b   # alef and alef madda
0628 0c   # be
062a 0f   # te and toe, dental
062b 11   # sin, se, suad
062c 12   # jim
062d 14   # bari he and he -- /h/, absent here
062e 15   # khe -- /x/, k until there is one
062f 16   # dal, dental
0630 18   # ze, zal, zuad, zoe
0631 19   # re, a tap
0632 18   # ze, zal, zuad, zoe
0633 11   # sin, se, suad
0634 1c   # shin
0635 11   # sin, se, suad
0636 18   # ze, zal, zuad, zoe
0637 0f   # te and toe, dental
0638 18   # ze, zal, zuad, zoe
0639 1d   # ain and hamza, both silent here
063a 1e   # ghain -- a voiced velar fricative
0641 1f   # fe
0642 7f   # qaf -- uvular, k until there is a q
0644 84   # lam
0645 86   # mim
0646 87   # nun
0648 89   # vao, which is also a vowel
064e 8f   # zabar, short a
064f 91   # pesh, short u
0650 90   # zer, short i
0679 10   # tte, retroflex -- t until T sounds
067e 0e   # pe
0686 13   # che
0688 17   # ddal, retroflex -- d until D sounds
0691 1a   # rre, the retroflex flap
0698 1b   # zhe
06a9 82   # kaf
06af 83   # gaf
06ba 88   # nun ghunna -- no nasal vowels yet
06be 8b   # do chashmi he, which makes the aspirates
06c1 14   # bari he and he -- /h/, absent here
06cc 8d   # ye, which is also a vowel
06d2 8e   # bari ye
